## SaMD Position — Coding

> **Position: Manual coding, text-selection pre-population, and practice-configured dictionary suggestions are in scope for Documents Management Core. AI automated code suggestions are out of scope and deferred to Phase 2.**
>
> **Rationale:**
> - **Manual Code Picker use** — the user directly searches and selects codes from the SNOMED hierarchy. No inference. Not SaMD.
> - **Text-selection pre-population** — text copied from the document to the Code Picker search box is a UI efficiency tool. No inference is performed; the user still searches and selects the code. Not SaMD.
> - **Practice-configured dictionary suggestions** — the practice administrator explicitly maps text strings to SNOMED codes. The system performs a deterministic string match (not AI/ML inference) and surfaces the pre-configured code as a suggestion. The user must explicitly accept each suggestion. This is rule-based, practice-controlled, and not SaMD.
> - **AI automated code suggestions** — automatically inferring SNOMED codes from document content without explicit rule configuration is in SaMD territory under MHRA guidance. Out of scope for Core. Deferred to Phase 2 pending MHRA SaMD assessment.
>
> **Constraints that must be maintained to preserve this position:**
> - Dictionary suggestions must never be auto-committed — explicit user confirmation required for every code before it reaches the patient record
> - Dictionary configuration is practice-controlled; the mapping is explicit and human-authored, not learned or inferred
> - The Code Picker writes codes to the patient record via the existing EMIS-X Terminology Service; this pathway must not be bypassed

