## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — all coding actions audited before committed to patient record
- **CLIN-005:** Clinical Decision Support Transparency — dictionary-based code suggestions must be clearly labelled as dictionary-matched and require explicit user confirmation before being added to the patient record
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — suggested codes must never be auto-committed; explicit user confirmation required
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — coding failures must fail closed; codes must not be partially written to patient record

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-039:** Incorrect clinical code added to patient record — wrong diagnosis or treatment code affects future clinical decisions
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low (manual Code Picker is an explicit user action; dictionary suggestions require confirmation)
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-040:** Dictionary suggestion accepted in an incorrect clinical context — a text string matches the dictionary and the corresponding code is suggested, but the code is clinically inappropriate for this specific patient or document instance
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low (requires either a misconfigured dictionary or the user confirming without reviewing the clinical context)
  - **Risk Level:** Medium — mitigated by mandatory explicit user confirmation and clear suggestion labelling

- **HAZ-DOC-041:** Code committed to wrong patient record — cross-reference with HAZ-DOC-032/038 from REQ-011/012
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Critical

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-038:** Dictionary suggestions never auto-committed; explicit per-code user confirmation required before any code reaches the patient record
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-039:** Dictionary suggestions clearly labelled as dictionary-matched; visually distinguished from manually searched codes; user must consciously accept each suggestion
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete (for transparency; user retains full accept/reject control)

- **MIT-DOC-040:** All coding actions audited before patient record write
  - **Type:** Observability
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

