## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — coding panel surfaces only the codes being added and the document being coded; full patient record not exposed
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — clinical codes written to patient record are special category data; encrypted at rest
- **IG-009:** Data Breach Notification — incorrect code on wrong patient record is a potential data quality/safety incident; detectable via audit

### Data Handling
- Clinical codes committed to patient record via EMIS-X Terminology Service (Code Picker); not bypassed
- Automated suggestion model inputs (document content) not stored beyond the coding session
- Audit entries record code added/removed by ERN; no plain NHS Number in logs

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 5(1)(d):** Accuracy — coding directly affects accuracy of patient clinical record
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — medical purposes

---

## Dimension 3: Security

### Applicable Guardrails
- **AUTH-004:** Authorization Required — coding endpoints require valid JWT with coding role scope
- **SEC-001:** TLS Encryption — all coding requests over TLS 1.2+

### Security Requirements
- Code commit scoped to authenticated user's practice and the specific patient being coded; cross-patient coding not permitted
- Code Picker integration uses existing EMIS-X Terminology Service authentication; no separate credential management required

