## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### KPIs
- Codes added per document (average, distribution)
- Text-selection usage rate (proportion of coding sessions where text-selection pre-population is used)
- Dictionary suggestion acceptance rate (proxy for dictionary quality and relevance)
- Dictionary suggestion rejection rate (proxy for dictionary noise or misconfiguration)
- Coding session duration (time from coding panel open to codes committed)
- Coding error rate (codes added then immediately removed — proxy for mistakes)

### OTEL Spans
- `documents.coding.session_started` — user opens coding panel for a document
- `documents.coding.text_selected` — user selects text in document viewer; selected text pre-populated into Code Picker search box
- `documents.coding.code_added` — code added to staging list (not yet committed)
- `documents.coding.code_removed` — code removed from staging list
- `documents.coding.problem_flag_set` — selected code marked as problem with significance level
- `documents.coding.code_comment_added` — comment added to staged code
- `documents.coding.observation_added` — observation added in coding flow
- `documents.coding.existing_problem_codes_viewed` — existing problem list viewed
- `documents.coding.dictionary_suggestion_presented` — dictionary-matched code suggestion presented to user
- `documents.coding.dictionary_suggestion_accepted` — user accepts a dictionary suggestion
- `documents.coding.dictionary_suggestion_rejected` — user rejects a dictionary suggestion
- `documents.coding.committed` — codes committed to patient record; count recorded
- `documents.coding.failed` — code commit failed; error type recorded

### SLOs
- Code commit: p95 < 2 seconds from user confirmation to codes written to patient record
- Dictionary suggestion presentation: p95 < 1 second from document load to dictionary suggestions surfaced (deterministic string match; not AI)
- Code commit success rate: ≥ 99.5%

